    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        182.347900390625,
        172.15890502929688,
        223.94789123535156
      ],
      "text": "disease",
      "font": "SegoeUI",
      "size": 32.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        257.3170166015625,
        527.4114379882812,
        271.7600402832031
      ],
      "text": "TB screening tools are designed to distinguish people with a higher probability of having TB disease",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        270.51702880859375,
        527.163818359375,
        284.9600524902344
      ],
      "text": "from those with a low probability and can be assumed to be free of TB disease. They are not intended",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.982686042785645,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        283.71697998046875,
        527.60205078125,
        298.1600036621094
      ],
      "text": "to provide a definitive diagnosis. In general, they need to be able to be implemented easily and relay",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.997849464416504,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        296.9169921875,
        527.3882446289062,
        311.3600158691406
      ],
      "text": "results rapidly in order to be informative in a screening context. Screening tests need to be followed",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        310.11700439453125,
        527.3859252929688,
        324.5600280761719
      ],
      "text": "by a diagnostic test, offered as part of a comprehensive clinical evaluation, to confirm or rule out TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        323.3170166015625,
        261.7978210449219,
        337.7600402832031
      ],
      "text": "disease in individuals who screen positive.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        345.0209045410156,
        527.467529296875,
        359.46392822265625
      ],
      "text": "The most desirable screening strategy would be one with a high total yield of true-positive cases of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        358.2209167480469,
        527.4310913085938,
        372.6639404296875
      ],
      "text": "TB, few false positives, low NNS, low cost, a rapid and simple algorithm and high client acceptability.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        371.4208984375,
        527.385986328125,
        385.8639221191406
      ],
      "text": "In practice, many of these factors tend to run in opposite directions, so a multifactorial analysis is",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        384.62091064453125,
        358.650390625,
        399.0639343261719
      ],
      "text": "needed to decide which screening tools and algorithms to use.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        406.3249206542969,
        527.6334838867188,
        420.7679443359375
      ],
      "text": "In 2014, WHO released a report summarizing the desirable characteristics, or target product profiles,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.998000144958496,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        416.73089599609375,
        527.298095703125,
        433.9679260253906
      ],
      "text": "(67) of screening tests for detecting TB disease  . The report highlighted that the minimal requirements",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.98969554901123,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        432.72479248046875,
        527.4509887695312,
        447.1678161621094
      ],
      "text": "for a target screening test would be an overall sensitivity of 90% and a specificity of 70% to detect",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        445.9248962402344,
        527.0986328125,
        460.367919921875
      ],
      "text": "pulmonary TB disease or rule it out in individuals being screened. Based on these benchmarks, an array",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.948982238769531,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        459.1249084472656,
        520.0783081054688,
        473.56793212890625
      ],
      "text": "of potential tools for screening for TB disease in different populations was considered by the GDG.",
